## Notes

| Topic | Advice |
|---|---|
| Query | Always $select; $expand only what you need; paging uses the nextLink exactly as returned |
| Throttling | Honour Retry-After; add jitter and concurrency limits |
| Token | Credential libraries cache tokens; do not fetch per request without caching |
| Secrets | Key Vault or managed identity or certificate, never source control |
| Errors | Log the error body and the request id header for support |

## Common mistakes

- Rebuilding the nextLink instead of following it.
- Using a licensed person's credentials.
- Unbounded parallelism that triggers throttling.
- Selecting all columns on wide tables.
